# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF, whatever platform commits.
# Without this, editing a file on Windows can rewrite every line ending and show
# the whole file as changed in `git status` — which makes a real one-line edit
# impossible to spot, and makes `git pull` look like a conflict when it is not.
* text=auto

# ...but `text=auto` above guesses, and a guess about a binary is destructive:
# a font that gets CRLF-normalised on checkout is a corrupt font, and the
# failure shows up as the page silently falling back to a system face rather
# than as an error. Name them binary so the guess never happens.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
